    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All 51 tests pass. The implementation is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI added a derived `telephoneDisplay` field that formats the stored E.164 telephone for humans while leaving raw `telephone` in E.164 form.\n\nThe codebase's pattern for read-time derived owner fields (e.g. `locality`, `contactPreference`, `ageBand`) is a `@Transient` getter on the `Owner` model that MapStruct auto-maps by name onto the OpenAPI-generated `OwnerDto`. I followed that exact pattern:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `readOnly` `telephoneDisplay` property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gets the getter/setter and it appears in JSON responses.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `@Transient getTelephoneDisplay()` that strips the `+`, splits off the country code (known codes `61`/`1` matched longest-first, otherwise a two-digit fallback), and renders `+<cc> <national digits grouped in threes>`. So `+61412345678` \u2192 `+61 412 345 678`. Returns `null` when there's no well-formed E.164 telephone.\n\nThe new `Cp37Tests` passes and all 51 tests remain green.",
